{"book":"lunyu","id":"sishu.lunyu.01","index":1,"passages":[{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.01","number":1,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"学","pinyin":"xué","traditional":"學","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"时","pinyin":"shí","traditional":"時","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"习","pinyin":"xí","traditional":"習","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"亦","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"说","pinyin":"yuè","traditional":"說","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"péng","traditional":"朋","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zì","traditional":"自","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"远","pinyin":"yuǎn","traditional":"遠","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fāng","traditional":"方","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"来","pinyin":"lái","traditional":"來","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"亦","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"乐","pinyin":"lè","traditional":"樂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"愠","pinyin":"yùn","traditional":"慍","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"亦","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Belajar dan selalu dilatih, tidakkah itu menyenangkan? (2) \"Kawan-kawan datang dari tempat jauh, tidakkah itu membahagiakan? (3) \"Sekalipun orang tidak mau tahu, tidak menyesali; bukankah ini sikap seorang Junzi - Kuncu?\"","translation_english":"1. The Master said, 'Is it not pleasant to learn with a constant perseverance and application? 2. 'Is it not delightful to have friends coming from distant quarters?' 3. 'Is he not a man of complete virtue, who feels no discomposure though men may take no note of him?'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.02","number":2,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xiào","traditional":"孝","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dì","traditional":"弟","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hǎo","traditional":"好","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fàn","traditional":"犯","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shàng","traditional":"上","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"鲜","pinyin":"xiān","traditional":"鮮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hǎo","traditional":"好","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fàn","traditional":"犯","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shàng","traditional":"上","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hǎo","traditional":"好","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zuò","traditional":"作","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"乱","pinyin":"luàn","traditional":"亂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"未","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"务","pinyin":"wù","traditional":"務","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"běn","traditional":"本","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"běn","traditional":"本","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"立","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shēng","traditional":"生","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"xiào","traditional":"孝","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dì","traditional":"弟","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wéi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"仁","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"běn","traditional":"本","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"！”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Youzi (Yucu) berkata, \"Seseorang yang dapat berlaku Bakti dan Rendah Hati, tetapi suka menentang atasan, sungguh jarang terjadi; tidak suka menentang atasan, tetapi suka mengacau, ini belum pernah terjadi. (2) \"Maka seorang Junzi - Kuncu mengutamakan pokok; sebab, setelah pokok itu tegak, Jalan Suci akan tumbuh. Laku Bakti dan Rendah Hati itulah pokok Peri Cinta Kasih.\"","translation_english":"1. The philosopher Yu said, 'They are few who, being filial and fraternal, are fond of offending against their superiors. There have been none, who, not liking to offend against their superiors, have been fond of stirring up confusion. 2. 'The superior man bends his attention to what is radical. That being established, all practical courses naturally grow up. Filial piety and fraternal submission!-- are they not the root of all benevolent actions?'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.03","number":3,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"qiǎo","traditional":"巧","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lìng","traditional":"令","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"sè","traditional":"色","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"鲜","pinyin":"xiān","traditional":"鮮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"仁","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"！”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang yang pandai memutar kata-kata dan bermanis muka, sesungguhnya jarang ber-Peri Cinta Kasih.\" (Shu Jing - Su King 11.3.1).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'Fine words and an insinuating appearance are seldom associated with true virtue.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.04","number":4,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zēng","traditional":"曾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"wú","traditional":"吾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rì","traditional":"日","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"sān","traditional":"三","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shěng","traditional":"省","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wú","traditional":"吾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shēn","traditional":"身","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"："},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谋","pinyin":"móu","traditional":"謀","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhōng","traditional":"忠","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"péng","traditional":"朋","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"友","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jiāo","traditional":"交","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xìn","traditional":"信","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？"},{"modern":"传","pinyin":"chuán","traditional":"傳","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"习","pinyin":"xí","traditional":"習","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Zengzi - Cingcu berkata, \"Tiap hari aku memeriksa diri dalam tiga hal: Sebagai manusia adakah aku berlaku tidak Satya? Bergaul dengan kawan dan sahabat adakah aku berlaku tidak dapat dipercaya? Dan adakah ajaran Guru yang tidak kulatih?\"","translation_english":"The philosopher Tsang said, 'I daily examine myself on three points:-- whether, in transacting business for others, I may have been not faithful;-- whether, in intercourse with friends, I may have been not sincere;-- whether I may have not mastered and practised the instructions of my teacher.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.05","number":5,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qiān","traditional":"千","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"chéng","traditional":"乘","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"国","pinyin":"guó","traditional":"國","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"jìng","traditional":"敬","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"事","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xìn","traditional":"信","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"节","pinyin":"jié","traditional":"節","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yòng","traditional":"用","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"爱","pinyin":"ài","traditional":"愛","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"shǐ","traditional":"使","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mín","traditional":"民","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"时","pinyin":"shí","traditional":"時","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Mengatur negeri yang mempunyai seribu kereta perang harus hormat kepada tugas dan dapat dipercaya, hemat dalam anggaran belanja dan mencintai sesama manusia, memerintah rakyat hendaklah disesuaikan dengan waktunya.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, To rule a country of a thousand chariots, there must be reverent attention to business, and sincerity; economy in expenditure, and love for men; and the employment of the people at the proper seasons.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.06","number":6,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"dì","traditional":"弟","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rù","traditional":"入","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xiào","traditional":"孝","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"chū","traditional":"出","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dì","traditional":"弟","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"谨","pinyin":"jǐn","traditional":"謹","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xìn","traditional":"信","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"fàn","traditional":"泛","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"爱","pinyin":"ài","traditional":"愛","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"众","pinyin":"zhòng","traditional":"眾","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"亲","pinyin":"qīn","traditional":"親","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"仁","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"行","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"余","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"餘","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"力","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"学","pinyin":"xué","traditional":"學","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wén","traditional":"文","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang muda, di rumah hendaklah berlaku Bakti, di luar hendaklah bersikap Rendah Hati, hati-hati sehingga dapat dipercaya, menaruh cinta kepada masyarakat dan berhubungan erat dengan orang yang berPeri Cinta Kasih. Bila telah melakukan hal ini dan masih mempunyai kelebihan tenaga, gunakanlah untuk mempelajari kitab-kitab.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'A youth, when at home, should be filial, and, abroad, respectful to his elders. He should be earnest and truthful. He should overflow in love to all, and cultivate the friendship of the good. When he has time and opportunity, after the performance of these things, he should employ them in polite studies.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.07","number":7,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xià","traditional":"夏","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"贤","pinyin":"xián","traditional":"賢","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贤","pinyin":"xián","traditional":"賢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"易","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"sè","traditional":"色","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"事","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mǔ","traditional":"母","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"néng","traditional":"能","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jié","traditional":"竭","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"力","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"事","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"néng","traditional":"能","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhì","traditional":"致","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shēn","traditional":"身","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"péng","traditional":"朋","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"友","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jiāo","traditional":"交","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xìn","traditional":"信","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"modern":"虽","pinyin":"suī","traditional":"雖","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"未","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"学","pinyin":"xué","traditional":"學","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"wú","traditional":"吾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bì","traditional":"必","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谓","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"謂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"学","pinyin":"xué","traditional":"學","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Cu-he berkata, \"Orang yang dapat menjunjung Kebijaksanaan lebih dari keelokan, melayani orang tua dapat mencurahkan tenaganya, mengabdi kepada pemimpin berani berkorban, bergaul dengan kawan dan sahabat kata-katanya dapat dipercaya; meskipun dikatakan ia belum belajar, aku akan mengatakan: ia sudah belajar.\" (S.S. IX: 18).","translation_english":"Tsze-hsia said, 'If a man withdraws his mind from the love of beauty, and applies it as sincerely to the love of the virtuous; if, in serving his parents, he can exert his utmost strength; if, in serving his prince, he can devote his life; if, in his intercourse with his friends, his words are sincere:-- although men say that he has not learned, I will certainly say that he has.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.08","number":8,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhòng","traditional":"重","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wēi","traditional":"威","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"学","pinyin":"xué","traditional":"學","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"gù","traditional":"固","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"zhǔ","traditional":"主","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhōng","traditional":"忠","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xìn","traditional":"信","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"友","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jǐ","traditional":"己","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"过","pinyin":"guò","traditional":"過","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wù","traditional":"勿","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"惮","pinyin":"dàn","traditional":"憚","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"gǎi","traditional":"改","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang Junzi - Kuncu bila tidak menghargai dirinya, niscaya tidak berwibawa; belajarpun tidak akan teguh. (2) \"Utamakanlah sikap Satya dan Dapat Dipercaya. (3) \"Janganlah berkawan dengan orang yang tidak seperti dirimu. (4) \"Bila bersalah janganlah takut memperbaiki.\" (S.S. IV:7; V:25).","translation_english":"1. The Master said, 'If the scholar be not grave, he will not call forth any veneration, and his learning will not be solid. 2. 'Hold faithfulness and sincerity as first principles. 3. 'Have no friends not equal to yourself. 4. 'When you have faults, do not fear to abandon them.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.09","number":9,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zēng","traditional":"曾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"shèn","traditional":"慎","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"终","pinyin":"zhōng","traditional":"終","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhuī","traditional":"追","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"远","pinyin":"yuǎn","traditional":"遠","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"mín","traditional":"民","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dé","traditional":"德","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"归","pinyin":"guī","traditional":"歸","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hòu","traditional":"厚","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Zengzi - Cingcu berkata, \"Hati-hatilah saat orang tua meninggal dunia dan janganlah lupa memperingati sekalipun telah jauh. Dengan demikian rakyat akan kembali tebal Kebajikannya.\" (S.S. II: 5).","translation_english":"The philosopher Tsang said, 'Let there be a careful attention to perform the funeral rites to parents, and let them be followed when long gone with the ceremonies of sacrifice;-- then the virtue of the people will resume its proper excellence.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.10","number":10,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qín","traditional":"禽","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"问","pinyin":"wèn","traditional":"問","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贡","pinyin":"gòng","traditional":"貢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fū","traditional":"夫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhì","traditional":"至","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"是","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bāng","traditional":"邦","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bì","traditional":"必","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"闻","pinyin":"wén","traditional":"聞","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhèng","traditional":"政","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"qiú","traditional":"求","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"抑","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贡","pinyin":"gòng","traditional":"貢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fū","traditional":"夫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"温","pinyin":"wēn","traditional":"溫","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"、"},{"pinyin":"liáng","traditional":"良","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"、"},{"pinyin":"gōng","traditional":"恭","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"、"},{"modern":"俭","pinyin":"jiǎn","traditional":"儉","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"、"},{"modern":"让","pinyin":"ràng","traditional":"讓","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dé","traditional":"得","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"fū","traditional":"夫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qiú","traditional":"求","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"诸","pinyin":"zhū","traditional":"諸","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"异","pinyin":"yì","traditional":"異","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qiú","traditional":"求","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Cu-khiem bertanya kepada Zi Gong - Cu Khong \"Tiap kali Guru tiba di suatu negara, niscaya mengetahui pemerintahannya. Ini disebabkan karena berusaha mengetahui atau diberi tahu?\" (2) Zi Gong - Cu Khong menjawab, \"Guru mendapatkan itu karena sikapNya yang ramah tamah, baik hati, hormat, sederhana dan suka mengalah. Demikianlah Guru mendapatkan pengetahuan itu. Berbeda dengan orang lainkah cara Guru mendapatkannya?\" (S.S. V:4).","translation_english":"1. Tsze-ch'in asked Tsze-kung, saying, 'When our master comes to any country, he does not fail to learn all about its government. Does he ask his information? or is it given to him?' 2. Tsze-kung said, 'Our master is benign, upright, courteous, temperate, and complaisant, and thus he gets his information. The master's mode of asking information!-- is it not different from that of other men?'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.11","number":11,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zài","traditional":"在","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"观","pinyin":"guān","traditional":"觀","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhì","traditional":"志","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"没","pinyin":"méi","traditional":"沒","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"观","pinyin":"guān","traditional":"觀","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"行","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"sān","traditional":"三","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"nián","traditional":"年","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"gǎi","traditional":"改","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谓","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"謂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xiào","traditional":"孝","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Pada saat ayah seseorang masih hidup, periksalah cita-citanya; setelah meninggal dunia, periksalah perbuatannya. Bila selama tiga tahun tidak mengubah Jalan Suci orang tuanya, boleh ia disebut seorang anak berbakti.\" (S.S. IV: 20).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'While a man's father is alive, look at the bent of his will; when his father is dead, look at his conduct. If for three years he does not alter from the way of his father, he may be called filial.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.12","number":12,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yòng","traditional":"用","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"和","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贵","pinyin":"guì","traditional":"貴","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"xiān","traditional":"先","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wáng","traditional":"王","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"sī","traditional":"斯","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"měi","traditional":"美","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"xiǎo","traditional":"小","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dà","traditional":"大","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yóu","traditional":"由","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"suǒ","traditional":"所","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"行","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"和","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"和","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"节","pinyin":"jié","traditional":"節","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"亦","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"行","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Youzi (Yucu) berkata, \"Di dalam menjalankan Tata Susila itu, keselarasanlah yang paling utama. Maka Jalan Suci raja-raja purba itu menyatakan, bahwa memang hal itulah terbaik untuk mengatasi perkara kecil maupun besar. (2) \"Kalau ada hal-hal yang tidak dapat dijalankan, inilah kalau orang hanya menjalankan keselarasan demi keselarasan raja, tanpa didasari Kesusilaan. Sudah barang tentu, ada hal yang tidak dapat dijalankan.\" (S.S. IV: 13).","translation_english":"1. The philosopher Yu said, 'In practising the rules of propriety, a natural ease is to be prized. In the ways prescribed by the ancient kings, this is the excellent quality, and in things small and great we follow them. 2. 'Yet it is not to be observed in all cases. If one, knowing how such ease should be prized, manifests it, without regulating it by the rules of propriety, this likewise is not to be done.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.13","number":13,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"xìn","traditional":"信","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jìn","traditional":"近","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"义","pinyin":"yì","traditional":"義","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"复","pinyin":"fù","traditional":"復","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"gōng","traditional":"恭","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jìn","traditional":"近","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"远","pinyin":"yuǎn","traditional":"遠","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"耻","pinyin":"chǐ","traditional":"恥","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rǔ","traditional":"辱","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"yīn","traditional":"因","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shī","traditional":"失","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"亲","pinyin":"qīn","traditional":"親","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yì","traditional":"亦","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zōng","traditional":"宗","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Youzi (Yucu) berkata, \"Kalau memegang sikap Dapat Dipercaya itu dilandasi Kebenaran, maka kata- katanya akan dapat ditepati. Kalau Sikap Hormat itu dilandasi Tata Susila, niscaya menjauhkan malu dan hina. Kalau dapat dekat kepada orang yang patut (karena jiwanya yang luhur), ia akan mendapatkan pembimbing yang boleh dijunjung.\"","translation_english":"The philosopher Yu said, 'When agreements are made according to what is right, what is spoken can be made good. When respect is shown according to what is proper, one keeps far from shame and disgrace. When the parties upon whom a man leans are proper persons to be intimate with, he can make them his guides and masters.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.14","number":14,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shí","traditional":"食","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qiú","traditional":"求","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"饱","pinyin":"bǎo","traditional":"飽","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"jū","traditional":"居","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qiú","traditional":"求","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ān","traditional":"安","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"mǐn","traditional":"敏","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"事","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shèn","traditional":"慎","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"jiù","traditional":"就","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhèng","traditional":"正","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yān","traditional":"焉","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谓","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"謂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hǎo","traditional":"好","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"学","pinyin":"xué","traditional":"學","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"已","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang Junzi - Kuncu, makan tidak mengutamakan kenyangnya; bertempat tinggal tidak mengutamakan enaknya, ia tangkas di dalam tugasnya dan hati-hati di dalam kata- katanya. Bila mendapatkan seorang yang hidup di dalam Jalan Suci, ia menjadikannya teladan meluruskan hati. Demikianlah seorang yang benar-benar suka belajar.\" (S.S. II: 15).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'He who aims to be a man of complete virtue in his food does not seek to gratify his appetite, nor in his dwelling place does he seek the appliances of ease; he is earnest in what he is doing, and careful in his speech; he frequents the company of men of principle that he may be rectified:-- such a person may be said indeed to love to learn.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.15","number":15,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贡","pinyin":"gòng","traditional":"貢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"贫","pinyin":"pín","traditional":"貧","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谄","pinyin":"chǎn","traditional":"諂","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"富","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"骄","pinyin":"jiāo","traditional":"驕","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"何","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"未","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ruò","traditional":"若","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贫","pinyin":"pín","traditional":"貧","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"乐","pinyin":"lè","traditional":"樂","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"富","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hǎo","traditional":"好","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贡","pinyin":"gòng","traditional":"貢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“《"},{"modern":"诗","pinyin":"shī","traditional":"詩","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"》"},{"pinyin":"yún","traditional":"云","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：‘"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qiè","traditional":"切","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"cuō","traditional":"磋","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zuó","traditional":"琢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mó","traditional":"磨","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"’，"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"sī","traditional":"斯","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谓","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"謂","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"赐","pinyin":"cì","traditional":"賜","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"shǐ","traditional":"始","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"《"},{"modern":"诗","pinyin":"shī","traditional":"詩","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"》"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"已","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"gào","traditional":"告","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"诸","pinyin":"zhū","traditional":"諸","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wǎng","traditional":"往","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"来","pinyin":"lái","traditional":"來","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Zi Gong - Cu Khong bertanya, \"Seorang yang pada saat miskin tidak mau menjilat dan pada saat kaya tidak sombong, bagaimanakah dia?\" Nabi menjawab, \"Itu cukup baik. Tetapi, alangkah baiknya bila pada saat miskin tetap gembira dan pada saat kaya tetap menyukai Kesusilaan.\" (S.S. XIV: 10) (2) Zi Gong - Cu Khong berkata, \"Di dalam Kitab Sanjak tertulis, 'Laksana dibelah, dikikir; laksana dipahat, digosok'. Demikianlah yang Guru maksudkan?\" Nabi Bersabda. \"0, Su; engkaulah orang yang dapat diajak membicarakan Kitab Sanjak; dengan Kubicarakan hal yang satu, kamu mengetahui kelanjutannya.\" (Shi Jing - Si King I.5.1.2).","translation_english":"1. Tsze-kung said, 'What do you pronounce concerning the poor man who yet does not flatter, and the rich man who is not proud?' The Master replied, 'They will do; but they are not equal to him, who, though poor, is yet cheerful, and to him, who, though rich, loves the rules of propriety.' 2. Tsze-kung replied, 'It is said in the Book of Poetry, \"As you cut and then file, as you carve and then polish.\"-- The meaning is the same, I apprehend, as that which you have just expressed.' 3. The Master said, 'With one like Ts'ze, I can begin to talk about the odes. I told him one point, and he knew its proper sequence.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.01.16","number":16,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"huàn","traditional":"患","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jǐ","traditional":"己","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"huàn","traditional":"患","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Jangan khawatir orang tidak mengenal dirimu, khawatirlah kalau tidak dapat mengenal orang lain.\" (S.S. XIV: 30).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'I will not be afflicted at men's not knowing me; I will be afflicted that I do not know men.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"}],"source_file":"03 - Lun Yu 論語/01 - Jilid I - Xue Er (Belajar) - 學而篇.md","title":"Jilid I — Xue Er (Belajar) · 學而篇"}
